# Tests (v5)

Rust tests run on the host with **`cargo test`** from the repo root (or `-p splatter`, `-p peaky-serve`, `-p peaky-geo`).

## Do this

- Run **`cargo test`** before marking seek, links, eligible-land, or splatter peak-scan work done.
- Add **timing assertions** on interactive hot paths (seek trim, peak scan, eligible build on small fixtures). Budgets live in test modules (`SEEK_TRIM_BUDGET`, `PEAK_SCAN_BUDGET`, etc.).
- Port v4 pytest coverage when touching the same behavior (`peaky-finders-v4/peaky_finders/tests/serve/test_seek_*.py`).

## Avoid

- Pipelines that boolean-intersect full-state eligible land during seek (use hop disc + viewport bbox; point-check sites/goals only).
- Silent multi-minute loops with no progress updates and no tests.

## Reference

v4 used `./peaky test` in Docker; v5 is pure Rust — no Docker test wrapper yet.
